1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:06,530
Exponential functions show up
all over the SAT math section.

2
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:10,740
A population that grows
by a percent each year.

3
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,900
A car that loses value.

4
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:15,129
A substance with a half-life.

5
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:19,460
They all use the same form, and
once you can read that form,

6
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:22,410
most of these questions get much faster.

7
00:00:22,818 --> 00:00:27,548
The most common mistake is mixing
up the rate and the factor.

8
00:00:27,978 --> 00:00:31,998
If something keeps sixty
percent of its value each year,

9
00:00:32,018 --> 00:00:35,318
it's decreasing by forty
percent, not sixty.

10
00:00:35,338 --> 00:00:38,638
We'll fix that, then work
through six practice questions,

11
00:00:38,658 --> 00:00:42,548
from quick reads to two hard
ones on equivalent forms.

12
00:00:43,068 --> 00:00:48,758
Here's the form: y equals
a times b to the t.

13
00:00:49,348 --> 00:00:52,768
a is the starting value,
the amount when t is zero.

14
00:00:52,788 --> 00:00:58,038
b is the growth factor, the number you
multiply by every time t goes up by one.

15
00:00:58,481 --> 00:01:01,700
If b is greater than
one, the quantity grows.

16
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,541
If b is between zero and one, it decays.

17
00:01:03,561 --> 00:01:04,561
That's the first thing to check
on any exponential question.

18
00:01:04,779 --> 00:01:06,400
Now the key translation.

19
00:01:06,419 --> 00:01:10,160
For growth, b equals one plus the rate.

20
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:14,120
A six percent increase
means b is one point oh six.

21
00:01:14,139 --> 00:01:17,720
For decay, b equals one minus the rate.

22
00:01:17,740 --> 00:01:21,910
A six percent decrease means
b is zero point nine four.

23
00:01:22,430 --> 00:01:25,850
And going backwards:
if b is one point two,

24
00:01:25,870 --> 00:01:29,370
the quantity increases by
twenty percent each period.

25
00:01:29,390 --> 00:01:34,200
If b is zero point seven five, it
decreases by twenty-five percent.

26
00:01:34,509 --> 00:01:37,370
Subtract from one to find the decrease.

27
00:01:37,390 --> 00:01:39,440
Don't read the decimal as the rate.

28
00:01:39,887 --> 00:01:44,697
The SAT also asks you to
tell exponential from linear.

29
00:01:44,807 --> 00:01:47,946
Linear means you add the
same amount each step:

30
00:01:47,966 --> 00:01:49,776
a constant difference.

31
00:01:49,847 --> 00:01:53,587
Exponential means you multiply
by the same number each step:

32
00:01:53,607 --> 00:01:55,216
a constant ratio.

33
00:01:55,657 --> 00:01:58,786
In word problems, listen for the units.

34
00:01:59,217 --> 00:02:02,827
Increases by fifty dollars
each year is linear.

35
00:02:03,057 --> 00:02:07,077
Increases by five percent
each year is exponential,

36
00:02:07,097 --> 00:02:10,427
because five percent of a bigger
amount is a bigger amount.

37
00:02:10,926 --> 00:02:14,265
Some quantities don't
change once per year.

38
00:02:14,285 --> 00:02:19,746
A half-life of six days means the amount
is multiplied by one half every six

39
00:02:19,766 --> 00:02:20,426
days.

40
00:02:20,446 --> 00:02:24,815
You write that as a times
one half, to the t over six.

41
00:02:25,326 --> 00:02:31,186
The exponent t over six counts how
many six day periods have passed.

42
00:02:31,206 --> 00:02:33,785
After eighteen days, that's three periods,

43
00:02:33,805 --> 00:02:36,815
so you multiply by one half three times.

44
00:02:36,926 --> 00:02:38,746
Doubling works the same way.

45
00:02:38,766 --> 00:02:41,986
Doubling every five hours is a times two,

46
00:02:42,006 --> 00:02:43,896
to the t over five.

47
00:02:44,426 --> 00:02:46,725
One more idea, for the hardest questions.

48
00:02:46,745 --> 00:02:49,886
The same growth can be written
in different time units,

49
00:02:49,906 --> 00:02:53,286
and the exponent tells you
which unit you're counting.

50
00:02:53,306 --> 00:02:55,636
We'll see that in questions four and five.

51
00:02:56,168 --> 00:02:58,387
Expect four kinds of questions.

52
00:02:58,407 --> 00:03:01,618
Interpret: what does a
number in the model mean?

53
00:03:01,848 --> 00:03:04,778
Build: which function
matches the description?

54
00:03:04,888 --> 00:03:07,988
Compare: is it linear or exponential?

55
00:03:08,008 --> 00:03:12,898
And rewrite: which equivalent form
shows a different rate or time unit?

56
00:03:13,168 --> 00:03:16,178
The rewrite questions
are usually the hardest.

57
00:03:16,666 --> 00:03:17,916
Question one.

58
00:03:17,946 --> 00:03:23,646
The function V of t equals twenty-four
hundred times zero point eight five to

59
00:03:23,666 --> 00:03:30,205
the t gives the value, in dollars, of a
laptop t years after it was purchased.

60
00:03:30,225 --> 00:03:34,756
Which statement best describes how
the value of the laptop changes?

61
00:03:35,201 --> 00:03:36,611
Pause and try it.

62
00:03:42,433 --> 00:03:45,093
The factor is zero point eight five.

63
00:03:45,113 --> 00:03:48,133
That's less than one, so the value decays.

64
00:03:48,153 --> 00:03:51,812
One minus zero point eight
five is zero point one five.

65
00:03:51,832 --> 00:03:54,892
The value drops by
fifteen percent each year.

66
00:03:54,912 --> 00:03:56,723
The answer is B.

67
00:03:57,218 --> 00:03:59,678
A reads the factor as the rate.

68
00:03:59,698 --> 00:04:04,478
C and D are dollar amounts, and
a constant dollar drop is linear.

69
00:04:04,498 --> 00:04:08,878
Three hundred sixty dollars is
fifteen percent of the starting value,

70
00:04:08,898 --> 00:04:11,238
but that's only the first year's drop.

71
00:04:11,258 --> 00:04:14,908
After that, it's fifteen
percent of a smaller number.

72
00:04:14,958 --> 00:04:17,577
And twenty-four hundred
is the purchase price,

73
00:04:17,597 --> 00:04:19,848
the value when t is zero.

74
00:04:20,279 --> 00:04:21,569
Question two.

75
00:04:21,879 --> 00:04:24,219
The table shows values of x and y.

76
00:04:24,239 --> 00:04:25,219
When x is zero, y is six.

77
00:04:25,239 --> 00:04:27,779
When x is one, y is nine.

78
00:04:27,799 --> 00:04:29,818
When x is two, y is thirteen point five.

79
00:04:29,838 --> 00:04:37,179
And when x is three, y
is twenty point two five.

80
00:04:37,199 --> 00:04:43,849
Which equation could represent
the relationship between x and y?

81
00:04:44,339 --> 00:04:45,749
Pause and try it.

82
00:04:52,571 --> 00:04:53,991
Check differences first.

83
00:04:54,011 --> 00:04:56,711
Six to nine is plus three.

84
00:04:56,731 --> 00:05:00,590
Nine to thirteen point five
is plus four point five.

85
00:05:00,610 --> 00:05:03,060
Not constant, so it isn't linear.

86
00:05:03,691 --> 00:05:05,231
Now check ratios.

87
00:05:05,251 --> 00:05:07,831
Nine over six is one point five.

88
00:05:07,851 --> 00:05:10,981
Thirteen point five over
nine is one point five.

89
00:05:11,001 --> 00:05:16,131
Constant ratio, so it's exponential,
with b equal to one point five.

90
00:05:16,671 --> 00:05:19,890
The starting value is y when x is zero,

91
00:05:19,910 --> 00:05:21,091
which is six.

92
00:05:21,111 --> 00:05:24,931
So y equals six times
one point five to the x.

93
00:05:24,951 --> 00:05:26,810
The answer is A.

94
00:05:26,830 --> 00:05:29,810
B fits only the first two rows.

95
00:05:29,830 --> 00:05:31,771
C swaps a and b.

96
00:05:31,791 --> 00:05:35,611
And D uses zero point five
for a fifty percent increase,

97
00:05:35,631 --> 00:05:37,561
which would make y shrink.

98
00:05:38,060 --> 00:05:42,080
Desmos shortcut: put the table
in Desmos and type y one,

99
00:05:42,100 --> 00:05:45,030
tilde, a times b to the x one.

100
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:50,720
Desmos runs an exponential regression
and reports a equals six and b equals one

101
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:51,789
point five.

102
00:05:52,283 --> 00:05:53,733
Question three.

103
00:05:53,803 --> 00:05:58,733
A sample of a radioactive substance
has a mass of eighty grams.

104
00:05:59,003 --> 00:06:02,333
The substance has a half-life of six days.

105
00:06:02,602 --> 00:06:05,703
Which function gives the mass M of t,

106
00:06:05,723 --> 00:06:09,493
in grams, of the substance
remaining after t days?

107
00:06:09,963 --> 00:06:11,373
Pause and try it.

108
00:06:18,195 --> 00:06:21,525
The sample starts at
eighty, so a is eighty.

109
00:06:21,554 --> 00:06:24,575
Half-life means multiply by one half.

110
00:06:24,595 --> 00:06:27,174
And that happens once every six days,

111
00:06:27,194 --> 00:06:30,215
so the exponent is t over six.

112
00:06:30,235 --> 00:06:32,165
The answer is D.

113
00:06:32,592 --> 00:06:36,972
Quick check: after six
days, t over six is one,

114
00:06:36,992 --> 00:06:38,572
so the mass is forty.

115
00:06:38,592 --> 00:06:40,162
Half of eighty.

116
00:06:40,272 --> 00:06:44,202
A would halve the mass
six times every day.

117
00:06:44,272 --> 00:06:47,282
B starts at forty instead of eighty.

118
00:06:47,312 --> 00:06:50,652
And C turns the six into
a six percent decrease,

119
00:06:50,672 --> 00:06:53,002
which isn't what half-life means.

120
00:06:53,542 --> 00:06:54,642
Question four.

121
00:06:54,662 --> 00:07:00,562
The function f of t equals fifteen
hundred times one point oh eight to the t

122
00:07:00,582 --> 00:07:05,072
models a quantity t years
after it was first measured.

123
00:07:05,302 --> 00:07:09,512
By what percent does the quantity
increase every two years?

124
00:07:09,940 --> 00:07:11,350
Pause and try it.

125
00:07:18,172 --> 00:07:22,261
Each year multiplies the
quantity by one point oh eight.

126
00:07:22,492 --> 00:07:26,592
Two years means multiplying
twice: one point oh eight squared,

127
00:07:26,612 --> 00:07:29,592
which is one point one six six four.

128
00:07:29,612 --> 00:07:33,551
That's an increase of sixteen
point six four percent.

129
00:07:33,571 --> 00:07:35,262
The answer is C.

130
00:07:35,696 --> 00:07:38,356
The trap is B, sixteen percent.

131
00:07:38,376 --> 00:07:42,626
Eight plus eight seems right,
but percent growth compounds.

132
00:07:42,696 --> 00:07:46,306
The second year's eight percent
applies to a bigger amount.

133
00:07:46,335 --> 00:07:48,636
D reads the factor as the percent.

134
00:07:48,656 --> 00:07:53,516
In fact, you could rewrite this function
as fifteen hundred times one point one

135
00:07:53,536 --> 00:07:56,206
six six four, to the t over two.

136
00:07:56,226 --> 00:07:59,836
Same function, counted
in two-year periods.

137
00:08:00,346 --> 00:08:01,606
Question five.

138
00:08:01,626 --> 00:08:07,886
The balance B of t, in dollars, of a
savings account is modeled by B of t equals

139
00:08:07,906 --> 00:08:11,805
two thousand times one
point oh six to the t,

140
00:08:11,825 --> 00:08:15,436
where t is the number of years
since the account was opened.

141
00:08:15,745 --> 00:08:20,676
Which function models the balance m
months after the account was opened?

142
00:08:21,196 --> 00:08:22,606
Pause and try it.

143
00:08:30,428 --> 00:08:32,528
Translate months into years.

144
00:08:32,548 --> 00:08:36,728
Twelve months is one year, so m
months is m over twelve years.

145
00:08:36,748 --> 00:08:41,928
Replace t with m over twelve: two
thousand times one point oh six,

146
00:08:41,948 --> 00:08:43,807
to the m over twelve.

147
00:08:43,827 --> 00:08:45,757
The answer is A.

148
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:48,380
Check it by plugging in twelve months.

149
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:54,179
In A, twelve over twelve is one, so the
balance is two thousand times one point

150
00:08:54,199 --> 00:08:55,100
oh six.

151
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:57,620
That's one year of growth, which is right.

152
00:08:57,640 --> 00:09:02,610
In B, twelve months would make the
exponent one hundred forty-four.

153
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:06,370
That's a hundred
forty-four years of growth.

154
00:09:06,810 --> 00:09:08,310
C is the tempting one.

155
00:09:08,330 --> 00:09:12,150
Six percent a year sounds
like half a percent a month.

156
00:09:12,170 --> 00:09:18,230
But one point oh oh five to the twelfth
is about one point oh six one seven,

157
00:09:18,250 --> 00:09:22,070
not one point oh six, because
monthly growth compounds.

158
00:09:22,090 --> 00:09:24,470
So C isn't equivalent.

159
00:09:24,490 --> 00:09:28,220
And D ignores the switch
to months completely.

160
00:09:28,641 --> 00:09:30,621
Last one, and the hardest.

161
00:09:30,641 --> 00:09:35,981
The mass, in grams, of a substance is
modeled by M of t equals one hundred

162
00:09:36,001 --> 00:09:40,700
twenty times zero point two
five, to the t over eight,

163
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:44,891
where t is the number of hours
since the start of an experiment.

164
00:09:45,241 --> 00:09:47,501
What is the half-life of the substance,

165
00:09:47,521 --> 00:09:48,771
in hours?

166
00:09:49,182 --> 00:09:50,402
Pause and try it.

167
00:09:50,422 --> 00:09:52,151
Take a little longer on this one.

168
00:10:00,955 --> 00:10:05,655
Zero point two five is one fourth,
and it applies every eight hours.

169
00:10:05,675 --> 00:10:09,094
So every eight hours, the
mass is cut to a quarter,

170
00:10:09,114 --> 00:10:10,094
not a half.

171
00:10:10,114 --> 00:10:11,775
That makes eight the trap.

172
00:10:11,795 --> 00:10:14,934
Cutting to a quarter is
the same as halving twice.

173
00:10:14,954 --> 00:10:19,285
So one halving takes
half as long: four hours.

174
00:10:19,805 --> 00:10:21,015
Here's the algebra.

175
00:10:21,285 --> 00:10:24,545
Rewrite zero point two five as one half,

176
00:10:24,565 --> 00:10:25,575
squared.

177
00:10:25,925 --> 00:10:29,184
Then one half squared,
to the t over eight,

178
00:10:29,204 --> 00:10:34,745
is one half to the two t over eight,
which is one half to the t over four.

179
00:10:34,765 --> 00:10:37,375
The half-life is four hours.

180
00:10:37,685 --> 00:10:38,815
Enter four.

181
00:10:39,272 --> 00:10:44,812
Desmos check: graph one hundred
twenty times zero point two five,

182
00:10:44,832 --> 00:10:48,731
to the x over eight, and
the line y equals sixty,

183
00:10:48,751 --> 00:10:50,761
which is half the starting mass.

184
00:10:50,911 --> 00:10:53,161
They cross at x equals four.

185
00:10:53,571 --> 00:10:57,140
Here's the method for any
growth or decay question.

186
00:10:57,251 --> 00:11:00,391
Step one: find a and b.

187
00:11:00,411 --> 00:11:01,911
a is the start.

188
00:11:01,931 --> 00:11:03,591
b is the multiplier.

189
00:11:03,611 --> 00:11:05,991
Step two: translate b.

190
00:11:06,011 --> 00:11:09,591
If it's greater than one, subtract
one to get the growth rate.

191
00:11:09,611 --> 00:11:13,781
If it's less than one, subtract
it from one to get the decay rate.

192
00:11:14,245 --> 00:11:16,705
Step three: read the exponent.

193
00:11:16,725 --> 00:11:22,654
t over k means one multiplication
every k units of time.

194
00:11:22,685 --> 00:11:25,544
Step four: when the time unit changes,

195
00:11:25,564 --> 00:11:29,544
substitute, then plug in
an easy value to check.

196
00:11:29,564 --> 00:11:32,415
And remember, percent changes compound.

197
00:11:32,445 --> 00:11:37,455
Never add them, and never split
them evenly across shorter periods.

198
00:11:37,918 --> 00:11:41,858
That's exponential growth and
decay: the starting value,

199
00:11:41,878 --> 00:11:45,937
the factor, the rate, and the
exponent that sets the time unit.

200
00:11:45,957 --> 00:11:49,897
For more practice, the College Board's
free Question Bank has plenty of these

201
00:11:49,917 --> 00:11:51,528
under Advanced Math.

202
00:11:52,022 --> 00:11:56,482
Every question in this video
was written for this video,

203
00:11:56,502 --> 00:11:59,352
in the style of the real test.

204
00:11:59,382 --> 00:12:01,682
Next up: SAT statistics.

205
00:12:01,702 --> 00:12:05,112
Mean, median, spread, and margin of error.

206
